description:
## Summary

Remove the separate `repl_reset` MCP tool. Session reset now happens through `repl` by sending Ctrl-D / EOF, including any remaining input that should run in the fresh session.

This PR:
- removes the `repl_reset` tool handler, schema, and dedicated tool-description file;
- updates docs, top-level help, and tool descriptions to present `repl` as the only public tool;
- updates install-time config cleanup so legacy `repl_reset` entries are stripped from `enabled_tools` and `disabled_tools`;
- updates integration, debug-event, sandbox-metadata, and session-management tests to use Ctrl-D reset behavior;
- keeps legacy `repl_reset` references only where they are needed for config migration or absence assertions.
